# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx reload [-k nodekey] [--key file] [--build dir target] [--status file]
          node image to
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx reload` builds <target> in the CMake tree <dir> with ninja, if `--build` is given, then calls <node>'s cpu server, as vx-cpu(1) does, with <image>'s directory as `/mnt/term/root`.
The session copies <image> to `<to>.new` and renames it to <to>, which the program's HotHost (hotreload(2)) sees and loads.

With `--status`, <file> is the program's status line, `image <v> loads <n> ...` (minimal-hot(4)'s `<image>.status`): the session waits, up to 3 s, for its load count to change or for a refusal, and prints `hot:` and the line.
vx then says how long it took from its start, the build included, to the new code running, as `reload.module_10k`, and fails if the image was refused or not taken.

`-k` and `--key` are vx-cpu(1)'s.

# EXAMPLES

```
vx reload --build build/amd64 hot10k \
    --status /data/hot/libminimalframe.so.status 127.0.0.1!27025 \
    build/amd64/kernel/libhot10k.so /data/hot/libminimalframe.so
```

# SEE ALSO

vx-cpu(1), hotreload(2), minimal-hot(4)

# DIAGNOSTICS

It exits 1 if the build fails, the session can't be made, or, with `--status`, the image wasn't taken.
